    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah i get that, but it feels like the \"ethical guidelines\" just slow everything down. if the tech can literally stop a crime or make things way smoother for everyone, shouldn't we just prioritize that instead of worrying about every single minor privacy risk or some theoretical bias? seems like we might be holding back progress for no good reason.",
